From 8c11dd4907e1a5f88c494ee868392d8a66aea751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:20:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] CA-430077: Low-privilege user can force-fail arbitrary
 tasks via task_id parameter

A low-privilege user could use [task_id] parameter in some APIs to set
other users' tasks failed. So now setting a task failed only if the task
is owned by the user (caller).

For a call or request, the check can be placed in the following 3
places alternatively:
1. Xapi_http.assert_credentials_ok if rbac_check is true in HTTP
   actions;
2. Server_helpers.do_dispatch if the call is a regular XenAPI call;
3. others by calling Xapi_http.with_context. This is a best-to-have
   place in case a call or request doesn't go to the 2 places above.

Includes unit tests for the task ownership check before setting the task
failed, and for client certificate sessions and root tasks: a client
certificate session has an empty auth_user_sid, the same as a root
session; check that it still can't own a task of root.

This is CVE-2026-119779, part of XSA-530.

Signed-off-by: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
Reviewed-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
Reviewed-by: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
